  "why_it_is_kept": "The cancel was sent in band to an active turn \u2014 `runtime_at_cancel: active`, `cancel_sent: true` \u2014 and the turn produced every one of the 400 lines it was asked for, finishing 6.5 seconds later with `stop_reason: end_turn`. So the run proves the runner can send a cancel to a live turn, and says nothing about whether this harness honours one. The tokens were spent and are charged. Attempt 2 cancels at four seconds into a count to 2000, and the receipt reads the streamed work back from the spool so the answer cannot be inferred from a stop reason again."
